"""ant-warm-cache — populate the gene_stats cache on this host.

The cache (``tmp/gene_stats_cache.db``) is populated lazily — every
``/api/gene_stats_all`` call writes new entries. ``ant-warm-cache``
fires those calls in bulk so a fresh deployment doesn't make the
first user pay the cold cost on every common gene.

Per-dataset distribution blobs (the heavy lift — ~800 ms layer scan
per dataset on first hit) are written when ANY gene query lands on
that dataset. Subsequent gene queries against the same dataset are
sub-millisecond bisect lookups. So warming with ~50 carefully-chosen
genes pre-builds every dataset's distribution and gets the catalog
to "any gene query is sub-second" state.

Adding a new dataset later: this script doesn't need to re-run. The
new dataset's distribution + per-gene rows fill in on first query.
Existing datasets' cache rows are untouched (independent (db_id,
gene_lc, fingerprint) keys).

Usage::

    ant-warm-cache                          # default panel, all filters off
    ant-warm-cache --genes APOE,TREM2,…     # custom list (CSV or @file.txt)
    ant-warm-cache --organism mouse         # filter to one organism
    ant-warm-cache --max 0                  # remove the budget cap

Runs against the LOCAL ant-serve on this host (rest_api_host /
rest_api_port from ``anthive.yaml``). Set ``--base-url`` to override.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import asyncio
import sys
import time

# Line-buffer stdout so per-gene progress lines flush in real-time
# when output is redirected (e.g. when the makefile target captures
# output, or when run under `tee`).
try:
    sys.stdout.reconfigure(line_buffering=True)
except (AttributeError, ValueError):
